---
description: TypeScript conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

- TypeScript strict mode
- Never use `any`
- Use ts-reset (`@total-typescript/ts-reset`)
- `no-unsafe-*` disabled
- ESM with bundler/Node resolution
- Never use CommonJS (`__dirname`, `__filename`, `require`, `module.exports`)
- ESM: `fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)` with descriptive names (`scriptDir`, not `__dirname`)
- Monorepo with `@repo/*` subpath exports
- Subpath exports (`@repo/utils/async`)
- Named exports (exception: Next.js pages/layouts)
- Type-only (`import type`)
- Interfaces for object shapes
- Types for unions/utilities/mapped/Zod inference
- Avoid enums (use const objects/union types)
- Infer types when possible (`type User = z.infer<typeof userSchema>`)
- Always camelCase variables
- Booleans with aux verbs (`isLoading`, `hasError`)
- Lowercase-with-dashes directories
- RORO (`({ name }: Input) => ({ id, name })`)
- Functional (avoid classes/decorators)
- Use `function` keyword for named function definitions, arrow functions for inline functions and React component methods
- Early returns (guard clauses): reduces nesting, keep success path at same indentation level, avoid else after early returns
- Single-line (`if (!value) return null`)
- Explicit return types for exported functions/API handlers
- Zod-first (validate at boundaries)
- Colocate schemas (`app/api/users/schema.ts`)
- Validation functions return results (never throw)
- Avoid unnecessary runtime validations in functions, we validate at build time
- Prefer inline expressions, minimize code without sacrificing readability
- No intermediate vars unless reused (`process(fetch())` not `const data = fetch(); process(data)`). Exceptions: destructuring, readability, error handling
- Lodash per-function (`import isEmpty from "lodash-es/isEmpty"`)

